reply.text:
The error means Spring cannot find a Spring bean for `MealMapper`. Make the mapper a Spring bean. Two common fixes:

1) If you use MapStruct: annotate the mapper interface so MapStruct generates a Spring component. Also enable the annotation processor in `pom.xml`.

Explanation: `@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")` tells MapStruct to generate an implementation that is a Spring bean.

`MealMapper` (`backend/src/main/java/dev/jclawlor/FitnessGoals/mapper/MealMapper.java`)
```java
package dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.mapper;

import org.mapstruct.Mapper;
import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.dto.MealDto;
import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.entity.Meal;

@Mapper(componentModel = "spring")
public interface MealMapper {
    Meal mapToMeal(MealDto dto);
    MealDto mapToMealDto(Meal meal);
}
```

Add MapStruct config to `pom.xml` (annotation processor):
```xml
<!-- add inside <dependencies> -->
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
  <artifactId>mapstruct</artifactId>
  <version>1.5.5.Final</version>
</dependency>

<!-- add to maven-compiler-plugin configuration -->
<plugin>
  <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
  <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
  <version>3.10.1</version>
  <configuration>
    <source>17</source>
    <target>17</target>
    <annotationProcessorPaths>
      <path>
        <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
        <artifactId>mapstruct-processor</artifactId>
        <version>1.5.5.Final</version>
      </path>
    </annotationProcessorPaths>
  </configuration>
</plugin>
```

2) If you don't want MapStruct: create a simple Spring component implementation of a mapper interface.

Explanation: a `@Component` implementation will be discovered by component scan and injected into `MealServiceImpl`.

`MealMapper` (`backend/src/main/java/dev/jclawlor/FitnessGoals/mapper/MealMapper.java`)
```java
package dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.mapper;

import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.dto.MealDto;
import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.entity.Meal;

public interface MealMapper {
    Meal mapToMeal(MealDto dto);
    MealDto mapToMealDto(Meal meal);
}
```

`MealMapperImpl` (`backend/src/main/java/dev/jclawlor/FitnessGoals/mapper/MealMapperImpl.java`)
```java
package dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.mapper;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.dto.MealDto;
import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.entity.Meal;

@Component
public class MealMapperImpl implements MealMapper {

    @Override
    public Meal mapToMeal(MealDto dto) {
        if (dto == null) return null;
        Meal meal = new Meal();
        meal.setId(dto.getId());
        meal.setName(dto.getName());
        // map other fields here
        return meal;
    }

    @Override
    public MealDto mapToMealDto(Meal meal) {
        if (meal == null) return null;
        MealDto dto = new MealDto();
        dto.setId(meal.getId());
        dto.setName(meal.getName());
        // map other fields here
        return dto;
    }
}
```

Either option will register a `MealMapper` bean and resolve the injection error.
